X pixmap frames: draw only what changed, and without blending an opaque page

The UI process redrew the whole view for every frame, so X composited the whole 32-bit frame
each time, though the web process sends the frame's damage. A frame in an X pixmap is top down,
so the damage is in the view's coordinates already: only those rectangles are queued for drawing
(the window keeps the rest of the frame before). Empty damage still redraws everything.

And for an opaque page the frame is composited with SOURCE, not OVER, so X doesn't read what is
under it first.
diff -ruN a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/gtk/AcceleratedBackingStore.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/gtk/AcceleratedBackingStore.cpp
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/gtk/AcceleratedBackingStore.cpp	2026-10-22 17:15:40.449299345 +0300
